.TH SYSLOG-SUMMARY 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syslog-summary \- count structure-verified syslog severities without messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syslog-summary
.RB [ --input " FILE|-" ]
.RB [ --format " auto|rfc3164|rfc5424" ]
.RB [ --null ]
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read a bounded, finite offline syslog input in classic BSD/RFC3164 or
RFC5424 format. Count only 0..7 severities from a valid leading numeric PRI
and matching envelope. PRI is facility times eight plus severity. Neither
message keywords nor embedded angle-bracket values count as priority.
Missing or invalid PRI/envelopes contribute to UNKNOWN (exit 1).
No log messages, identities, paths or structured-data values are emitted.
Does not invoke syslog utilities, open host logs by default or modify files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read one ordinary readable file, or stdin (default). Rejects symlinks.
.TP
.BI --format " auto|rfc3164|rfc5424"
Select expected message structure (auto by default).
.TP
.B --null
Emit ten records, each with exactly three NUL-terminated fields, no heading.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show usage and exit successfully.
.TP
.B --version
Print command name and version.
.SH OUTPUT
Columns PRIORITY, LEVEL and COUNT. Eight priority rows plus UNKNOWN and
TOTAL rows. Results are aggregates, not message samples.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Complete input; every record had a recognized priority (or input was empty).
.TP
.B 1
Complete input, but one or more rows had an absent/unverifiable PRI or header.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 3
Unreadable/symlink input, blank/truncated records, or input limits exceeded.
No partial success-shaped output is produced.
.SH LIMITS
Maximum 16 MiB input, 128 KiB physical line and 50,000 records. A nonempty
input must end with LF. Ordinary local syslog files commonly omit PRI and
therefore produce UNKNOWN, not a guessed severity. No --follow.
The sending application can choose PRI; the report is not intrusion detection.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B printf '%s\\n' '<34>Oct 21 08:30:04 host app: sample' | syslog-summary
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journal-summary (1),
.BR log-summary (1)
